    "html": "<p>A rigid vessel contains an ideal gas at a pressure of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span>. Three-quarters of the gas is removed from the vessel. The temperature of the remaining gas is then increased until the root-mean-square (r.m.s.) speed of the molecules is doubled.</p>\n<p>What is the new pressure of the gas?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{P}{2}\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"B\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"C\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2P\"></span></p></li><li data-label=\"D\"><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4P\"></span></p></li></ol>"
  },
